# Plugins, streamed

::toc[On this page]

This document is fed to the parser a few characters at a time. Edit it, or any other file, and it streams again. Turn off _streamed_ above the preview and the same files compile to a Svelte component instead, as they do in a build.

## A chart

:::chart[The Label](type=bar)
- One: 100
- Two: 80
- Three: 60
- Four: 40
:::

`plugins/chart` draws the list as bars. The frame is there when the container opens, a name shows as it is typed, and a bar grows once its line has ended.

## A directive

`directives/counter.svelte` is the component of :counter[3], named after its file. It is drawn before its paragraph has ended, and keeps its count once it has.

## A plugin with a directive

:lookup[markdown] and :lookup[opcodes] are shown at once. `plugins/lookup/plugin.js` looks each one up, and the answer patches a block that has already rendered. `lookup.svelte` beside it is the component.

## A plugin on every heading

Each heading got its link when its line ended, from `plugins/heading_links/plugin.js`.

## A plugin from npm

The list at the top is `@mdsvex/plugin-toc`, which `plugins/toc/plugin.js` exports. It grows as each heading arrives.

- a list
- with *strong*, _emphasis_ and `code`

> _new plugin_ in the plugins menu above the editor makes one: a plugin file and the component of its directive, registered as you type.
